senses.gloss:
amanuṣya, subst. m. and adj. (cf. next and amānuṣa; as subst. = Pali amanussa; in Skt. only Lex. and Pāṇ. 〔2.4.23〕),
(1) subst. spirit, demon; SP 〔83.9〕; in lists of kinds of creatures, in cpd. SP 〔169.2〕 deva-nāga-yakṣa-gandharvāsura-garuḍa-kiṃnara-mahoraga-manuṣyāmanuṣyais; SP 〔69.5—6〕; same list as separate words Gv 〔141.24〕 devān … manuṣyān amanuṣyān; Mv 〔ii.107.13〕, read with mss. anyā kiṃnarīṇāṃ gatiḥ, amanuṣyāṇām, different is the path of the k˚, who are demons (or, as adj., superhuman); amanuṣya-vyādhi, disease caused by a demon or spirit, Mv 〔i.253.11 ff.〕; 〔284.6 ff.〕; 〔287.5〕; amanuṣya-upasarga (so prob. read, as cpd., with one ms.), id., Mv 〔i.287.17〕; ˚ṣyābhisṛṣṭa Bbh 〔63.6〕;
(2) adj., superhuman: Mv 〔ii.30.16〕 ˚ṣyāṇi ca gītavādyaśabdāni (so with mss.; Senart amānu˚).

amānuṣa, m.
(1) = amanuṣya(ka), subst.: Divy 〔456.21〕 (see s.v. amanuṣyaka); LV 〔75.15〕;
(2) n. of a nāga king; Māy 〔247.26〕.
